  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c42647c6b8ce4362a57878c870c2a6cc, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::RaceMapRegionHover
  raceName: ???
  factionName: The Shifting Confluence
  territoryName: The Living Expanse
  culturalIdentity: "Evolution  \u2022  Adaptation  \u2022  Survival"
  territoryDescription: 'Beyond the familiar boundaries of civilization lies the Living Expanse, a vast and unsettling territory where the distinction between nature and living flesh has nearly disappeared.

    Strange forests pulse with biological energy. Enormous organic structures rise from the earth, while rivers of unusual fluids flow through landscapes that appear to breathe and shift.

    The environment is constantly evolving, with new growths emerging as older formations decay or transform.

    Within this alien wilderness dwell the MutaBorn, an extraordinary race of organisms whose bodies possess an unnatural capacity for adaptation and mutation.

    Some resemble humanoid creatures, while others display monstrous forms, exposed musculature, hardened biological armor, additional limbs, or symbiotic growths.

    Despite their terrifying appearance, the MutaBorn possess intelligence, individuality, and desires as varied as those of any other civilization.'
  factionHistory: 'The true origins of the MutaBorn remain one of the world''s greatest mysteries.

    Ancient records contain scattered references to creatures capable of reshaping their own bodies, but no surviving account explains when or how the race first emerged.

    Some scholars believe they originated from experiments involving unstable magical and biological substances.

    Others suggest they are the descendants of organisms that evolved under extraordinary environmental conditions.

    Among the MutaBorn themselves, stories of their origins vary just as dramatically.

    What is known is that their unusual biology made coexistence with other civilizations extraordinarily difficult.

    Feared for their appearance and unpredictable abilities, many MutaBorn were hunted, imprisoned, or subjected to experimentation.

    Others were exploited for the rare biological materials their bodies could produce.

    Over time, increasing numbers of MutaBorn migrated toward the strange wilderness now known as the Living Expanse.

    There, they established communities among environments that would prove deadly to most other races.

    Unlike conventional kingdoms, MutaBorn society is not defined by a universal government or a rigid system of laws.

    Instead, communities form around shared biological characteristics, mutual survival, powerful individuals, and complex symbiotic relationships.

    Some seek peaceful coexistence with neighboring civilizations.

    Others harbor deep resentment toward the races responsible for generations of persecution.

    And within the darkest reaches of the Living Expanse, certain organisms have begun exhibiting mutations unlike anything previously recorded.

    Whether these changes represent the next stage of their evolution or the emergence of something far more dangerous remains unknown.'
  available: 0
  concealed: 1
  raceTitle: {fileID: 1692440425}
  factionTitle: {fileID: 788844904}
  territoryTitle: {fileID: 1112252920}
  identityTitle: {fileID: 1880740373}
  statusTitle: {fileID: 932152335}
  loreBody: {fileID: 886993393}
  loreScroll: {fileID: 2134004245}
